<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-bus" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1431?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>What Germany thinks of carmaker Audi's $4 billion deal with Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1d29970f9dcbc12d2b418a241f1fd2d4d8503aa3df91ca0c87a69da288ea989</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479--6c6f86b95e86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The luxury carmaker is set to open its first factory in the United States — a move Trump credits to his tariffs. DW examines the German reaction amid a massive auto industry cull at home.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany revive its economy before the far-right AfD gains ground?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be720353ce3fd2564d65a12476f755d1f2db5190d80e3f05216f8c02ca1f9dad</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-far-right-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102--ac9492c7777a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-far-right-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Can new growth sectors create jobs and ease voters' economic fears, thereby helping contain the far-right AfD?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions target Iran's rail sector as Tehran shifts cargo from sea routes to overland corridors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3d0ddcab93f6e5078927f29fe7e130b1285a8d614b48e0006a4b05ce669b235</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413--6d742d0c6640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As US sanctions expand to Iran's rail sector, Tehran is relying more heavily on overland links with China and Central Asia. But capacity constraints, delays and costs limit rail's ability to replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why US investors are snapping up Germany's famed Mittelstand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aea909c72ee94b85155f6bae76dbb8b7802c470a5c0db64328b97334da1ad5a1</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421--453454d6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Increasing amounts of US capital are flowing into Germany's traditional industrial firms and family-owned businesses. As many business owners struggle to find successors, more companies are becoming acquisition targets.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU promotes sovereign, trusted AI as it struggles to catch US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fdb1be8ad86d6b5a2489812702a5b247acd623c0f3f000d745cb6801b241a60</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770--286aee32e70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At an international AI summit in Dublin, EU leaders promoted trusted and independent artificial intelligence. Critics question whether the bloc can close the gap with the US and China while maintaining strict regulation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Chinese tech brands are outpacing Western rivals from EVs to robot vacuums</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f64456a20d8af49d1ddda7c082591606e8df8d889038bb96fd9252d1e6ece87</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-chinese-tech-brands-are-outpacing-western-rivals-from-evs-to-robot-vacuums/a-79646187--a8751d31a3ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-chinese-tech-brands-are-outpacing-western-rivals-from-evs-to-robot-vacuums/a-79646187?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From action cameras and smartphones to EVs and robot vacuums, Chinese brands are gaining ground worldwide, despite privacy and security concerns. What's driving their rise, and can European rivals keep up?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's diesel deal with Russia is unlikely to significantly lower global fuel prices despite expectations of rapid relief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f65f1f545b8dce1407900ca78865fec6d3f0fb545f86059e110981f3f325ab9</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expect/a-79659601--8934faa2519e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expectations-of-rapid-relief/a-79659601?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the world's largest diesel exporter, the US benefits from high prices. At home, however, consumers are feeling the strain of rising living costs. Why Donald Trump's deal with Russia is unlikely to change that.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93dd6e695c0f9c57d3949dbcb09e09682c32efc42a989732fc143bb0548df6f3</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Finland, the world's happiest nation, faces a glum winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a72caf66f13e33c5217740252c2283278b977f7c1c47d24cc9ba328f8f25d5a8</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348--0df829428818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finns have many reasons to feel content, but the country's pile of debt is not one of them. Russia's war in Ukraine has added to the fiscal burden. Can the Nordic nation absorb another shock?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How a multibillion-dollar oilfield has ignited the UK-Argentina feud over the Falklands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5612428c658a43fc3e50fdd45a18aaa30e23970fcc9d2832e18453903c5b2fe8</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973--b9ae4084dbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentina and the UK once fought a war over the Falkland Islands. Now, the multibillion-dollar Sea Lion oil project has reignited old tensions, with Buenos Aires seeking to put a stop to the plans.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8eb16350cbcd4d74ea5d111361c36af95d79acdec65cdc8ab9a2995af4bd44b4</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Euro plummets against US dollar: Has the next financial crisis begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4673f0d93510e0fdc8869f2f4605eb824f4fd3d4cc2e9928276cd82510808bc</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031--86ee12acb8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The euro has fallen to a 17-month low against the dollar. That will make inflation worse in the EU, where political worries and concern over French debt are already troubling investors. Is a fiscal crisis at hand?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Stock market scandal hits half a million investors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc0dfc20345a3d4deed882e7483ea7c604cc52ff549162f4946cc7bc17b70204</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710--a0311f00dcbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Asset managers are alleged to have artificially inflated the value of their funds. Turkish authorities have made multiple arrests, and a leading AKP lawmaker has resigned.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could see drivers pay higher running costs while also increasing carbon emissions.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf52047f82a3d986324c12a3f028c66e083b636bdb2ab57b6fb3e3bb69b4a19b</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-/a-79496554--0804b7619722.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-costs-while-also-increasing-carbon-emissions/a-79496554?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could yet see drivers pay higher running costs while increasing planet-heating emissions.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9264e1e66e3a98d09feeb539a51ffbf90caf24a3a9d90d2f2256d494ca51c8d2</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afaafec661164d9b8604bc98e0274ab32fefc65acddba3e89cc146ccf14c1343</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643--538fe77d9a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past six years, COVID, two wars and Donald Trump's tariffs have shaken world trade. With globalization already stalling, is this a temporary shock or the start of a great reversal?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Diesel prices are surging putting further pressure on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b095e4ac70c42214267eb5a14e378d123ebf938728a9cad32670e92929d9a8bd</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992--edb37306aa00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trucks, farms and industry are powered with diesel. Now prices are soaring due to refinery disruptions, supply shortages and geopolitical tensions. A potential US export ban could make Europe's diesel crunch even worse.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>China's new travel rules unsettle tech giants and talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d864776c469ec4b318233a91d8c8841b5e347dcab2f6be2770e90fe6a77618cb</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937--16d904ca4025.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing is locking the gates to stop expertise and capital in strategic industries from fleeing. The country accused of industrial-scale intellectual property theft now fears the West will take its own.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Will Germany have enough gas this winter amid energy supply crunch?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:109c0a73935418f020cbd3d469980618c020b32ceed92f5cd759e3a274005222</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317--cfd94c55c93d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage sites are far less full than in recent years. Officials say supplies are secure, but analysts warn that a cold winter or import disruptions could push prices higher. So how secure is the supply?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's car crisis: Can the 35-hour workweek survive?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d6e757bf782ffca632557df20d628d63149a19c695ddad2e3141e77cb0bf617</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488--cb2e3220b33e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German carmakers want employees to work 40 hours instead of the current 35 without extra pay, arguing it would improve competitiveness. Unions strongly oppose the proposal and view it as an attack on workers' rights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
